    "text": "Suppose that P is a finite p-group with a non-trivial partition (which is\nequivalent to having proper Hughes subgroup Hp (P ) := ⟨g ∈ P | g p ̸= 1⟩ ̸= P ). If P\nadmits a fixed-point-free automorphism of prime order, must P be of exponent p?\n                                                                                 M. Lewis",
